<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Keychain access for the MYND-329 quick-unlock Touch ID provider
    (core/src/plugins/quick_unlock/apple.rs — moved out of the desktop crate and
    generalized macOS -> macOS + iOS per decisions.md 2026-07-12). Without this
    entitlement on a SIGNED binary, storing/reading a biometric-gated
    (kSecAccessControlBiometryCurrentSet) Keychain item fails with
    errSecMissingEntitlement (-34018).

    That OSStatus is mapped to ProviderError::HardwareUnavailable (MYND-628), so
    an unsigned build reports "biometric unavailable" and falls back to the
    password instead of surfacing an opaque backend error.

    The access group is the app's own identifier (self-access). With a real
    Apple Development / Developer ID certificate, prefix it with the team:
    `<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)md.myne.desktop</string>`. With ad-hoc
    signing (`codesign -s -`) the literal identifier below is used.

    LOAD-BEARING on macOS 26+: a restricted entitlement is only honored when a
    provisioning profile that authorizes it is embedded. Without the profile,
    AMFI refuses to spawn the app ("Launchd job spawn failed", POSIX 163) even
    though a `codesign` verify pass and notarization checks pass; with the
    entitlement stripped instead, the Keychain returns errSecMissingEntitlement
    (-34018) at runtime. `bundle.macOS.files` embeds
    `Myne_Mac_Development.provisionprofile` at Contents/embedded.provisionprofile
    so both halves hold. The profile is device-bound (only registered Macs launch
    the bundle) and expires; regenerate it with the macOS signing section of
    `operations/runbooks/local-multiplatform-build.md` when it goes stale.

    NOTE: `tauri dev` runs an UNSIGNED binary, so biometric still fails there.
    These entitlements apply to `tauri build` (configured via
    bundle.macOS.entitlements) or when the dev binary is signed manually.
  -->
  <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
  <array>
    <string>D8UWYY2KY7.md.myne.desktop</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
